        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-08T18:31:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is going to cause analysis failures and broken build if anything is checked into the tree that uses `cc_device_for_host` and the build is run without `ART_USE_SIMULATOR`.  What is the purpose of this check?",
      "revId": "5641b97b8bfbc9b7da162dbb8144791523fd5fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "585aa1f4_4a6ab170",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3406,
      "author": {
        "id": 1989777
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T14:21:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is used to restrict use of the module to the ART simulator specific modules that we need this for, similar to the way that `java_device_for_host` is restricted to a few projects where it is needed. This way we also ensure that production builds are not affected by this change.\n\nI don\u0027t think there is a technical reason this guard couldn\u0027t be expanded or removed altogether however I think that can be done in the future as and when someone wants to use it.",
      "parentUuid": "6702e611_5e42616c",
      "revId": "5641b97b8bfbc9b7da162dbb8144791523fd5fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82476bea_5d0ab45b",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3406,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-10T17:12:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I assume you\u0027re planning to check in some uses of `cc_device_for_host` to AOSP.  If so, won\u0027t that immediately break the normal builds that don\u0027t set `ART_USE_SIMULATOR`?",
      "parentUuid": "585aa1f4_4a6ab170",
      "revId": "5641b97b8bfbc9b7da162dbb8144791523fd5fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "819a7c69_ff23e1af",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3406,
      "author": {
        "id": 1989777
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-11T09:43:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No because those uses are only enabled when `ART_USE_SIMULATOR` is set, see  https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/art/+/2680026/14/runtime/Android.bp#694 for the only uses of this module. Those modules are in turn only ever used when the simulator is enabled as the regular .S entrypoint files are used otherwise.",
      "parentUuid": "82476bea_5d0ab45b",
      "revId": "5641b97b8bfbc9b7da162dbb8144791523fd5fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8edf653c_c8d44030",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 3406,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T17:31:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see, you\u0027re requiring that all `cc_device_for_host` modules use a product config variable keyed off of `ART_USE_SIMULATOR` to disable themselves.\n\nI\u0027m fine with keeping it as is, but also consider whether that complexity is adding any value.  Having `cc_device_for_host` modules enabled when `ART_USE_SIMULATOR` is not set shouldn\u0027t cause any problems.\n\nIf you do remove the conditional I\u0027d suggest adding checks in neverallow.go to restrict the usage of `cc_device_for_host` to the art directories.",
      "parentUuid": "819a7c69_ff23e1af",
      "revId": "5641b97b8bfbc9b7da162dbb8144791523fd5fc3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
